Planning and Development Office
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282
(Fax) 307-637-6366

MEMO

To:
Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins and Members of the City Council
From:
Jeanie Shrednik, PLA, Parks and Greenway Planner and Member of the Belvoir
Steering Committee

Subject: "A RESOLUTION TO EFFECTUATE APPROPRIATE PROPERTY RECORD
CORRECTIONS, AUTHORIZING THE MAYOR TO EXECUTE ALL
NECESSARY
DOCUMENTS
RELATED
TO
AMENDING
AND
EXTINGUISHING CERTAIN EASEMENT AGREEMENTS AFFECTING A
PORTION OF THE BELVOIR RANCH AND THE PROPERTIES DIRECTLY
NORTH AND SOUTH OF THAT PORTION OF THE BELVOIR RANCH."

Date:
December 6, 2024

Background:

The item for consideration is an authorization from Council to allow the Mayor with the support
of City staff to amend access easements north of the Robert Green property to meet actual access
road conditions and to extinguish the City’s public trail easement that was gifted to the City by
Mr. Green in 2015. (City Contract #6431).

City staff and members of the Belvoir Steering Committee, to include myself, Vicki Nemecek,
Seth Lloyd, Charles Bloom, Jack Studley, Stefanie Boster, John Brodie, Tom Cobb, and Brent
Lathrop (The Nature Conservancy) met on December 5, 2024, to discuss the matters of both the
road access easements through the Armstrong and City owned properties north of the Green
property as well as the trail easement that was gifted to the City by Mr. Green in 2015. All agreed
that is was appropriate to recommend to the Governing Body that it authorize the Mayor to execute
the necessary documents amending the access road easements and extinguishing the trail easement.
This action would allow Mr. Green to sell his property and is also in the best interests of the City.
The changes will address significant deviations between the use of the current roads, which do not
align with the attendant legal access authority. The changes would also allow the City to refocus
its finite resources and funding on the existing 20,000 acres already owned by the City, to include
the design and negotiation of a railroad crossing to the Big Hole. This access is one of the key
objectives for the Belvoir property.

The City recently received an appraisal for the Green property, dated November 15, 2024. The
appraisal was for 667 acres of land and a residence. The property appraised for $2,085,000.00.  Per

  Planning and Development Department
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282 (Fax) 307-637-6366
```

### Page 2 of 14

```text
Mr. Green and family, a prospective buyer has offered $3.5 million for the property but the City's
trail easement causes significant concern.  This is understandable since it would be difficult if not
impossible to keep public users within this easement and not have them wandering on other parts
of the private property, which property is already encumbered by a conservation easement.

If the City were to consider purchasing the Green property, it would likely have to match or exceed
what is being offered by the prospective buyer and the purchase would not provide any better
chances of crossing the railroad than what exists now on the City owned property.  Further, the
trail easement on Mr. Green’s property is not necessary for providing trail access to the Big Hole,
which can be accessed directly through City owned property. Finally, Mr. Green's easement across
the City's property to the north does not specify maintenance responsibilities for that access. Were
the City to agree to extinguishing the trail easement, in return the City could clarify that the owner
of the Green property is responsible for maintenance on that access and not the City.

The Belvoir Steering Committee recommends approval of this resolution allowing the Mayor with
the support of City staff to adjust the existing access easements to the north of the Green property,
and to extinguish the trail easement on the Green property in response to appropriate concessions
or consideration by the owners.

Enclosures:
Record of Survey/Map
Easement Agreement between Robert E. Green Sr. Living Trust, August 11, 2015, Contract
#6431
