### Page 3 of 14

```text
RESOLUTION NO. _____________

ENTITLED:  "A RESOLUTION TO EFFECTUATE APPROPRIATE PROPERTY
RECORD CORRECTIONS, AUTHORIZING THE MAYOR TO EXECUTE
ALL NECESSARY DOCUMENTS RELATED TO AMENDING AND
EXTINGUISHING CERTAIN EASEMENT AGREEMENTS AFFECTING
A PORTION OF THE BELVOIR RANCH AND THE PROPERTIES
DIRECTLY NORTH AND SOUTH OF THAT PORTION OF THE
BELVOIR RANCH."

WHEREAS, the Belvoir Ranch is owned by the City of Cheyenne. a section of which (the
"Ranch Property"), is located between the Union Pacific Railroad (UPRR) to the south,
Interstate 80 generally to the north and more particularly Harriman Road to the north/northwest.
Other sections of the Belvoir Ranch lie south of the UPRR, as does the majority of the Big Hole
property, which borders the state of Colorado;

WHEREAS, David Armstrong, et ux, are the owners of the property directly to the North
of the Ranch Property (the "Armstrong Property");

WHEREAS, Harriman Road runs across the northwest portion of the Armstrong Property.
The City has an access easement across the Armstrong Property along the southwestern section,
allowing access from Harriman Road to the northern portion of the Ranch Property;

WHEREAS, over time the physical route for the City’s use of the access easement across
the Armstrong Property has notably deviated from the original access route granted by the owners
of the Armstrong Property, resulting in the use of a road that does not align with the City's legal
access authority;

WHEREAS, the owners of the Armstrong Property have agreed to work with the City to
address this issue by modifying the City's easement in order for the City's physical access to be
in-line with the underlying legal authority. Modifying the easement is in the best interests of both
the City and the owners of the Armstrong Property;

WHEREAS, the owners of the Armstrong Property are willing to modify the current
easement if the City agrees to install a fence along the eastside of the modified easement to create
a buffer between the City's access and the Armstrong Property;

WHEREAS, the Robert E. Green, Sr. Living Trust is the owner of the property directly to
the South of the City’s Ranch Property (the "Green property"), for which the City's predecessor in
interest granted a private access easement across the Ranch Property;

WHEREAS, over time the physical route for accessing the Green Property has deviated
significantly from the original route of access granted by the City's predecessor in interest resulting
in the use of a road that does not align with legal access authority for the Green Property;
9:41 am, Dec 06, 2024
```

### Page 4 of 14

```text
Page 2 of 2

WHEREAS, the private access easement for the Green Property is silent on the
maintenance responsibilities for that access and it is in the interests of the City and the owners of
the Green Property to clarify those maintenance responsibilities;

WHEREAS, the owner of the Green Property wishes to amend the current access
agreement to more accurately reflect its current use;

WHEREAS, the City executed an easement agreement with the owners of the Green
Property, which easement provides the City with access across the Green property for public trails
and related accommodations. The easement was gifted to the City and the City did not provide any
financial consideration for the trails easement;

WHEREAS, the City's public trails easement across the Green property has not aided or
otherwise assisted the City with access issues more largely affecting the Belvoir Ranch and is not
necessary for any other purpose;

WHEREAS, the City does not have the ability to maintain the easement, were it to be
developed for public trails. Further, it is in the interest of the City to clarify the maintenance
responsibilities for the private access easement to the Green Property; and

WHEREAS, it is in the best interests of the City to vacate or extinguish the public trails
easement on the condition that the maintenance responsibilities for the private access easement to
the Green Property are clearly assigned to the owners of that property.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY
OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that the Mayor is hereby authorized to execute any and all
necessary documents related to extinguishing, amending or otherwise modifying the easements as
provided in this resolution to effectuate the intent as herein stated.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED THIS ______ DAY OF __________________,
2024.

__________________________________________
Patrick Collins, Mayor

(SEAL)

ATTEST:

____________________________________
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
```

